  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` to follow `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (5 of 5).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js` with roughly 150 cases. They cover:\n- **Range syntax:** x-ranges, partial versions with operators, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges and `||`.\n- **Prerelease rules:** ordering and the same-tuple rule.\n- **Invalid input:** malformed versions and ranges return `false`.\n\n- **Big numbers:** Version numbers are compared as `BigInt`, so very large values compare exactly.\n- **No throwing:** The function never throws, including for non-string input.\n- **Prereleases in partial versions:** The spec doesn't say what to do with a prerelease on a partial version such as `1.2-beta`. I treat it as an invalid range, so it returns `false`.\n- **Wildcards with comparison operators:** The spec doesn't cover `>*` or `<*`. I made them match nothing, and `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.",
